# Engineering Standards

¶ - Code quality bar, product shape, workspace practice and the source header profile. Routed from the global policy ¶11; read before writing or reviewing code.

document:
  id: taks.engineering@1
  version: 1
  status: proposed
  authority_basis: [@taks/global-policy]
  scope: identity, code_standards, product_shape, workspace_practice, header_profile, context_comment_profile, templates
  excludes: language_grammar, delegation, sdd_lifecycle

¶ 1 — Identity

```text
signature {{SIGNATURE_AUTHOR}} # optional; empty -> line omitted
tagline {{SIGNATURE_TAGLINE}} # default "VAI CORINTHIANS!"
org {{OPERATOR_ORG}}
mission {{OPERATOR_MISSION}}
```

¶ 2 — Code Standards

```text
ban god_object, monolith
contracts small, explicit, testable
errors explicit_errors > panics in libraries
doc_comment every public function and type
tests {{TEST_STANCE}}
end_of_plan output the execution model plus a one-sentence justification
```

¶ 3 — Product Shape

```text
pattern {{PRODUCT_SHAPE}} # operator default stack; empty -> follow the project
fallback consult local AGENTS.md
non_destructive original source files are never mutated
integration reuse the existing application layer
```

¶ 4 — Workspaces

```text
rule read local AGENTS.md before proposing changes
focus strictly per package (crate, module, project)
large_workspace -> compact context in long sessions; clear between unrelated packages
structural_change_completed -> build or check the touched package (e.g. `cargo check -p <crate>`)
```

¶ 5 — Source Header Profile

Presentation profile for source code, not TDSL semantics. Delimiter-agnostic:
`<D>` is each file's own comment delimiter. `{{KERNEL_HOME}}/scripts/diagram_check.py`
owns the delimiter table and renders every banner; never write one by hand.

```text
target all_source_files
delim // Rust C C++ C# JS TS Go Java Kotlin Swift
delim #  Python Ruby Shell PowerShell Makefile TOML
delim -- SQL Lua Haskell
delim /* */ CSS SCSS
delim <!-- --> HTML XML SVG
skip [.json .yaml .toml .md .env .lock .tdsl]

anchor § registry marker
  header_use `§ - <purpose one line> · <lang>`, no number
  chapter_use `§ <n> — <DOMAIN> — <observable responsibility or result>`
  subsection_use `§ <n>.<m> — <Domain> — <observable responsibility or result>`
glyph ─ U+2500 header rule; ── flanks chapter titles
rule_width 44
number l1=integer l2=integer.integer
title l1=UPPERCASE l2=TitleCase
title_rule domain classifies the responsibility; description lets an agent decide whether to read it
ban_title [UTILS HELPERS MISC LOGIC METHODS] when used without a specific observable responsibility
anchor_language_rule chapters live at module level, column zero; never nested inside a block
```

```text
header ln: |
  <D> ────────────────────────────────────────────
  <D> [PROJECT] [VERSION] — [Filename.ext]
  <D> § - [Purpose one line] · [Language]
  <D> [SIGNATURE_AUTHOR] # omitted when empty
  <D> [SIGNATURE_TAGLINE] # omitted when empty
  <D> ────────────────────────────────────────────

chapter_l1 ln: |
  <D> ── § 1 — SECTION NAME — Brief description ──

chapter_l2 ln: |
  <D> ── § 1.1 — Subsection Name — Brief description ──
```

Procedure and guard rules belong to skill(diagram).

¶ 6 — Semantic Context Comment Profile

`※` marks a deliberate, indexable source comment. Ordinary comments remain local and are not
part of the preliminary context map. The marker is optional; when present, its claim must remain
current and must be verified against source before an agent treats it as behavior.

```text
form `<D> ※ <kind> — <one current verifiable statement>`
location full-line comment inside the § chapter it qualifies
language English

kind assumption information accepted locally but not proven here
kind boundary exclusive authority or responsibility
kind decision chosen approach and the materially relevant rejected alternative
kind effect externally visible mutation or interaction not obvious from the local signature
kind invariant condition a distant or tempting local change must preserve
kind rationale non-obvious reason the implementation has this shape
kind relation stable reference to another responsibility
kind risk known limitation or failure exposure

comment_when rationale_not_derivable | distant_invariant | exclusive_authority |
  non_obvious_order | external_effect | material_assumption | material_risk | rejected_alternative
ban_comment restates_code | repeats_section_title | narrates_history | substitutes_for_clear_code |
  vague_reason | unowned_todo
rule one marker one proposition
rule references use stable file and § identity, never line number
rule public API documentation uses the language native doc-comment form; `※` only adds non-local context
rule stale_or_conflicting_comment -> code wins, report divergence, repair only within authorized scope
```

```text
examples:
  `<D> ※ invariant — Generated directories never enter the source index.`
  `<D> ※ boundary — This module is the only writer of project-map.json.`
  `<D> ※ rationale — Imports establish dependency evidence, not execution order.`
  `<D> ※ relation — Supplies indexed sections to @flowchart/projector § 2.`
```

¶ 7 — Templates

```text
dir {{KERNEL_HOME}}/templates/
  project-AGENTS.md.template human resume entry, natural language
  AGENTS.md.template agent-facing TDSL; local and non-derivable only, inherits global
  briefing.template subagent executor TDSL, <~400 tokens, points to the spec
  cross-model-prompt.template self-contained, no references to this ecosystem

dir {{KERNEL_HOME}}/skills/<skill>/template.tdsl
  owner the skill of the same name
  rule authoring shape only; the type contract belongs to the schemas
  rule loaded only when its skill is invoked
```
